{"analysis":"Version 0 sends far too many neutral comments to negative: 136 of 320 neutral texts, against 160 kept neutral. In this dataset annotators reserve negative for a clear personal emotion: despair, fear or sadness, insults and curses, or the claim that the numbers are lies. Many other comments look critical but are labelled neutral:
- demands and orders (close borders, test more, publish villages, bring back measures, resign);
- 'why' questions to the institute;
- suggestions;
- scolding careless citizens or cafes;
- sarcasm about testing ('no tests, no cases');
- 'league table' jokes about cities being on top;
- 'ma gjall' cheering of numbers.

Neutral-to-positive errors (24) come from wishes or relief that the annotators treat as neutral, such as 'Dhasht Zoti me pak raste' (God grant fewer cases), 'Edhe pak e iku virusi' (a little more and the virus is gone) and 'Prishtina n Top form' (Prishtina in top form). Positive itself is noisy, though, so I only add that sports-style jokes about cities leading the numbers are not positive.

The main change is to make neutral the default and to raise the bar for negative: criticism, demands or complaints phrased as advice, a question or a joke stay neutral. Negative still keeps curses, lie accusations, explicit sadness or fear, and despair about Kosovo. I keep the rule that praise mixed with criticism counts as positive.","question":"Does this Facebook comment on the Kosovo public health institute's COVID-19 post express a clear emotional stance (warm approval/hope versus hostility/distress), or is it mainly informational, practical or joking?","rule":"Neutral is the default and the largest class. Demands, suggestions, requests for data, 'why' questions, criticism of careless citizens or cafes, sarcasm about testing, jokes about cities 'leading the league', and 'ma gjall' cheering are all neutral, even when phrased sharply. Negative needs explicit hostility or distress: calling the numbers lies or a farce, curses or insults, or stated sadness, fear, despair or exhaustion. Positive needs clear praise, thanks, blessings or relief; praise mixed with criticism is still positive.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Praise or thanks to doctors or the institute, blessings, wishes for recovery, explicit relief or joy at recoveries or falling cases.","examples":["Respekt per punen tuaj (Respect for your work)","Sherim te shpejt per te gjith. (Quick recovery to all.)","Mos e ndrroni prej ndrrimit qit doktor se mir pi hec (Don't change this doctor from the shift, he's doing well)","Mashallah kofshin me ymer (Mashallah, may they live long)"],"cues":"bravo (well done), respekt (respect), ju lumt (well done), faleminderit (thanks), Zoti ju bekoft (God bless you), sherim (recovery), shyqyr (thank God), kofshin me ymer (may they live long)","not_for":"Wishes for fewer cases, or jokes about a city being 'on top', are neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Name tags, jokes, banter, statistics, questions, requests for details, demands for measures or more tests, advice and criticism of citizens without insult or despair.","examples":["Mbyllni kufinjt mos luani me jetet e njerzve (Close the borders, don't play with people's lives)","Pse nuk po perputhen rastet e juaja me ato raste qe i raportoni ne OBSh???? (Why don't your cases match those you report to WHO????)","Nëse nuk bëjmë asnjë test, s'do të kemi asnjë rast. U zgjidh problemi. (If we do no tests, we'll have no cases. Problem solved.)","Vushtria on top çdo nat (Vushtrria on top every night)"],"cues":"pse (why), testoni (test), publikoni (publish), mbyllni (close), kthene karantinen (bring back quarantine), ma gjall (livelier), on top, hahaha, personal names","not_for":"Explicit 'lies', curses, 'turp' aimed at the institute, or stated sadness or fear are negative."},"negative":{"what":"Claims that the numbers are lies or invented, curses and insults, explicit sadness, fear, despair or exhaustion, bitter hopelessness about Kosovo.","examples":["Krejt Rrena (All lies)","Trishtim, 15 vdekje edhe dje. (Sadness, 15 deaths yesterday too.)","Bergamo e ballkanit jena bo ka 13 persona me vdek tmer i zotit osht (We've become the Bergamo of the Balkans, 13 people dying, it's God's horror)","Si gjithcka tjeter  edhe COVID 19 do te deshtoj ne Kosove (Like everything else, COVID 19 will fail in Kosovo too)"],"cues":"rrena/gënjeshtra (lies), hajgare (farce), zoti ju vraft (God curse you), flaka ju dalt (may you burn), trishtim (sadness), tmerr (horror), na lodhet (we're exhausted), magari (donkey)","not_for":"Practical demands, data questions, scolding people to wear masks, or sarcastic jokes without insult are neutral."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 2 swung too far toward negative: 158 neutrals were called negative, and macro-F1 fell to 67.8. Version 1, with only 15 such errors but 88 negatives called neutral, scored best at 72.0. The model responds sharply to wording, so version 3 needs a deliberate middle line.

New neutral errors in version 2 mostly came from texts with only implicit criticism:
- demands for lockdowns or borders;
- requests for villages, ages or data;
- 'why' questions;
- comparisons with Italy, Germany or Albania;
- sarcasm about low testing;
- scolding citizens who skip masks;
- city 'league' and 'jackpot' banter;
- name tags and gibberish.
The broad cues 'mockery', 'sarcasm' and 'boll' (enough) pushed these into negative.

Negatives that version 1 missed carried an explicit marker:
- blame or fault words: faj (fault), qeveria koti (the Kurti government, used mockingly);
- claims that the numbers are invented: aparati (the machine), copy paste, 5000 numra (5000 numbers);
- explicit fed-up words: bajat (stale), lodhet (tired), merzit (fed up), spo na intereson (we don't care);
- insults: injoranta (ignorant), pisa (dirty one), ju raft (may it hit you);
- fear or despair: katastrof (catastrophe), tmerr (horror), deshtim (failure).

Plan: make neutral the default for requests, proposals, questions, comparisons and banter, even when they are critical or sarcastic. Require negative to show an explicit hostility or distress marker: blame, a fabrication claim, an insult, a fed-up statement or fear. Keep the positive criterion from version 2, which recalled 85 of 109 positives.","question":"Does this Facebook comment on the Kosovo public health institute's COVID-19 post express warm approval or hope, an explicit hostile or distressed feeling, or neither (information, requests, suggestions, banter)?","rule":"Neutral is the default. Requests for data, 'why' questions, demands for measures or more tests, comparisons with other countries, scolding of mask-skippers, sarcasm about testing and city 'league' banter stay neutral, even when critical. Choose negative only when the comment shows an explicit marker: assigning blame or fault, claiming the numbers are invented or fake, insulting people, saying they are fed up or tired, or expressing fear, horror or despair. Positive needs praise, thanks, relief at good numbers or hope for zero cases; praise mixed with criticism is still positive.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Praise or thanks to doctors or the institute, congratulations, hope or prayers for no cases, cheering at recoveries.","examples":["Respekt per punen tuaj (Respect for your work)","shpresoj qe ta kalojmë këtë gjendje me sa më pak pasoja. (I hope we get through this with as few consequences as possible.)","Ajde ma gjall ma gjall t sherum (Come on, more and more recovered)"],"cues":"bravo (well done), respekt (respect), faleminderit (thanks), urime (congratulations), shpresoj (I hope), inshallah (God willing), asnje rast (no cases), mir (good)","not_for":"'Ma gjall' cheering of new infections is neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Tags, statistics, observations, requests for details, questions, proposals, mask reminders, comparisons, jokes and banter, including mildly critical or sarcastic ones.","examples":["Mbyllni kufinjt mos luani me jetet e njerzve (Close the borders, don't play with people's lives)","Nëse nuk bëjmë asnjë test, s'do të kemi asnjë rast. U zgjidh problemi. (If we do no tests, we'll have no cases. Problem solved.)","Pse ka Mitrovica Verit nuk po jepni Rezultate hiq !? (Why aren't you giving any results for North Mitrovica!?)","Jeckpoot...vushtri e dhezi..apet (Jackpot... Vushtrri lit up again)"],"cues":"personal names, publikoni (publish), testoni (test), mbyllni (close), pse (why), ma gjall (livelier), on top, hahaha","not_for":"Explicit blame, claims of fake numbers, insults, being fed up, or fear are negative."},"negative":{"what":"Blame of government or citizens, claims the numbers are invented, insults, fed-up frustration, fear or despair.","examples":["Qeveria koti ika fajet (The Kurti government is to blame)","Veq shifren e par pja ndrroni se tekstin tjeter veq copy paste po get (You only change the first number, the rest is copy paste)","U ba bajat me ka 200 mo  ndrrone pak (It's stale with 200 a day, change it a bit)","Krejt Rrena (All lies)"],"cues":"faj (blame), rrena (lies), aparati (the machine), bajat (stale), lodhet (tired), merzit (fed up), injoranta (ignorant), katastrof (catastrophe), tmerr (horror), deshtim (failure)","not_for":"Requests, proposals, questions or banter without such a marker are neutral."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 6 (80.1) moved errors toward neutral. Negative recall fell from 126 to 120, and 46 negatives were called neutral against 25 neutrals called negative.

The cause was narrowing negative blame to 'blame of the authorities'. Several gold negatives blame citizens or gatherings in fault language or warn of disaster:
- 'Namazi i Kurban Bajramit i ka fajet' (the Bajram prayer is to blame);
- 'per te pandergjegjeshmite... burg' (for the irresponsible... prison);
- 'Njerezit po dalin pa kontroll' (people are going out uncontrolled);
- 'ka mu ba katastrof' (there will be a catastrophe);
- 'ma shum prej frikes' (more from fear).

So I restore blame of anyone, including citizens, gatherings and Bajram, and name fear of catastrophe as negative. The distinction from neutral scolding is the fault, punishment, disaster or out-of-control framing, versus calm advice or proposals.

I keep version 6's positive fixes, which corrected the government-defence texts ('Në asnjë rast nuk mundemi ta fajsojm qeverin' (we can't blame the government at all), 'Tybe... qeveria koti po punon shum' (the Kurti government is working hard)). I also keep the not_for for ironic 'hajr' and 'ma gjall' over case counts. The aim is to land between versions 5 and 6.","question":"Does this Facebook comment on the Kosovo public health institute's COVID-19 post express warm approval or hope, an explicit hostile or distressed feeling, or neither (information, requests, suggestions, banter)?","rule":"Neutral is the default. Data requests, 'why' questions, demands for measures, comparisons, calm advice to stay home, sarcasm about testing and city 'league' banter stay neutral, even when critical. Choose negative for an explicit marker: blaming anyone (government, citizens, gatherings), a claim the numbers are fake, an insult or curse, a call to punish people, a fed-up statement, fear of catastrophe or loss of control, or bitter irony that Kosovo fails. Positive needs praise or defence of doctors, the institute or the government, thanks, relief, or sincere hope for zero cases; praise mixed with criticism stays positive.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Praise, thanks or defence of doctors, the institute or the government; congratulations; sincere hope or prayers for no cases; cheering at recoveries.","examples":["Respekt per punen tuaj (Respect for your work)","Në asnjë rast nuk mundemi ta fajsojm qeverin por secili duhet fajsu vehten (In no way can we blame the government, everyone should blame themselves)","shpresoj qe ta kalojmë këtë gjendje me sa më pak pasoja. (I hope we get through this with as few consequences as possible.)","Ajde ma gjall ma gjall t sherum (Come on, more and more recovered)"],"cues":"bravo (well done), respekt (respect), faleminderit (thanks), urime (congratulations), shpresoj (I hope), inshallah (God willing), asnje rast (no cases), po punon shum (is working hard)","not_for":"Ironic 'hajr' or 'ma gjall' over new cases, city-ranking banter, bare good-news headlines are neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Tags, statistics, observations, requests for details, questions, proposals, calm advice, comparisons, jokes and banter, including critical or sarcastic ones.","examples":["Mbyllni kufinjt mos luani me jetet e njerzve (Close the borders, don't play with people's lives)","Nëse nuk bëjmë asnjë test, s'do të kemi asnjë rast. U zgjidh problemi. (If we do no tests, we'll have no cases. Problem solved.)","213 ja pafshim hajrin (May we see good from these 213)","Jeckpoot...vushtri e dhezi..apet (Jackpot... Vushtrri lit up again)"],"cues":"personal names, publikoni (publish), testoni (test), mbyllni (close), pse (why), ma gjall (livelier), on top, hahaha","not_for":"Blame, fake-number claims, insults, calls to punish, being fed up, or fear of catastrophe are negative."},"negative":{"what":"Blame of government, citizens or gatherings, claims the numbers are invented, insults or curses, calls to punish, fed-up frustration, fear or despair, bitter irony about Kosovo failing.","examples":["Namazi i Kurban Bajramit i ka fajet per shtimin e rasteve (The Kurban Bajram prayer is to blame for the rise in cases)","Veq shifren e par pja ndrroni se tekstin tjeter veq copy paste po get (You only change the first number, the rest is copy paste)","Futne more ma shpejt kosoven ne karantin sepse ka mu ba katastrof e madhe (Put Kosovo in quarantine fast, a big catastrophe is coming)","Krejt Rrena (All lies)"],"cues":"faj/fajet (blame), rrena/prralla (lies/fairy tales), aparati (the machine), bajat (stale), lodhet (tired), magari (donkey), pisa (dirty one), injorantat (the ignorant), burg/denim (prison/punishment), pa kontroll (out of control), katastrof (catastrophe), frike (fear), Kotit (Kurti's, mocking)","not_for":"Requests, proposals, calm advice, questions or banter without such a marker are neutral; praise of the government is positive."}}}

{"analysis":"Same plan as before, with the wording trimmed to stay under 400 words:
- restrict approving words next to name tags to explicit approval, not nicknames or slang;
- restore 'praise mixed with criticism stays positive';
- note that praising the Kurti government is positive.","question":"Does this Facebook comment on the Kosovo public health institute's COVID-19 post express warm approval or hope, an explicit hostile or distressed feeling, or neither (information, requests, suggestions, banter)?","rule":"Neutral is the default. Data requests, 'why' questions, demands for measures, proposals to fine people, comparisons, serious scolding of citizens, sarcasm about testing and city 'league' banter stay neutral, even when critical. Choose negative only for an explicit marker: blame, a claim the numbers are fake, an insult or curse, a fed-up statement, or the commenter's own fear or despair. Positive needs praise or defence of doctors, the institute or the government, thanks, relief, sincere hope for zero cases, or an explicit approving word, even next to a name tag; praise mixed with criticism stays positive.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Praise, thanks or defence of doctors, the institute or the government; congratulations; sincere hope for no cases; cheering at recoveries; explicit approving words.","examples":["Respekt per punen tuaj (Respect for your work)","Në asnjë rast nuk mundemi ta fajsojm qeverin por secili duhet fajsu vehten (In no way can we blame the government, everyone should blame themselves)","shpresoj qe ta kalojmë këtë gjendje me sa më pak pasoja. (I hope we get through this with as few consequences as possible.)","Ali Kastrati mire (Ali Kastrati, good)"],"cues":"bravo (well done), respekt (respect), faleminderit (thanks), urime (congratulations), shpresoj (I hope), inshallah (God willing), asnje rast (no cases), super, nice, mire (good), perher (always), vazhdojm (let's keep going), rrnoft (long live)","not_for":"Ironic 'hajr' or 'ma gjall' over new cases, city-ranking banter, and tags with nicknames or slang ('GG', 'bruno') are neutral. Praising 'qeveria koti' (the Kurti government) is positive."},"neutral":{"what":"Bare tags, statistics, observations, requests for details, questions, proposals, scolding without insults, comparisons, jokes and banter, including critical or sarcastic ones.","examples":["Mbyllni kufinjt mos luani me jetet e njerzve (Close the borders, don't play with people's lives)","Nëse nuk bëjmë asnjë test, s'do të kemi asnjë rast. U zgjidh problemi. (If we do no tests, we'll have no cases. Problem solved.)","Po shihet qe njerezit nuk jane te diciplinuar (It's clear people aren't disciplined)","213 ja pafshim hajrin (May we see good from these 213)"],"cues":"personal names alone, publikoni (publish), testoni (test), mbyllni (close), pse (why), ma gjall (livelier), on top, hahaha","not_for":"Blame, fake-number claims, insults, being fed up, or own fear are negative."},"negative":{"what":"Blame, claims the numbers are invented, insults or curses, fed-up frustration, fear or despair, bitter irony about Kosovo failing.","examples":["Qeveria koti ika fajet (The Kurti government is to blame)","Veq shifren e par pja ndrroni se tekstin tjeter veq copy paste po get (You only change the first number, the rest is copy paste)","U ba bajat me ka 200 mo  ndrrone pak (It's stale with 200 a day, change it a bit)","Krejt Rrena (All lies)"],"cues":"faj (blame), rrena/prralla (lies/fairy tales), aparati (the machine), bajat (stale), lodhet (tired), magari (donkey), pisa (dirty one), injorantat (the ignorant), ju raft (may it strike you), tmerr (horror), deshtim (failure)","not_for":"Requests, proposals, serious scolding, questions or banter without such a marker are neutral."}}}
